  "counter": false,
  "note": "Story mit App-Karten als Beweisfuehrung: Slide 2 der Tag (Trade-Liste), Slide 4 der Monat (Kalender), Slide 5 das Muster (Win Rate nach Trade-Nummer). Risiko pro Trade bleibt in derselben Groessenordnung wie die anderen Trades. Zahlen konsistent: Tag 9. = +120 -60 +250 -860 = -550; Monat = +2.260 gruen, -3.750 rot = -1.490; 6 rote Tage, 5 davon mit viertem Trade.",
  "caption": "Trades one, two and three were on the list. They followed the plan and they finished +$310. Trade four was opened at 12:20 — 40 minutes after the session was supposed to be over — and it cost -$860. The day closed at -$550.\n\nThat part every trader remembers. The next part is the one nobody has: the month. Six red days. Five of them had a fourth trade. The green days almost never did.\n\nAcross 214 trades the first three of a session win 64% of the time. From the fourth on, it drops to 31%. Same trader, same setups, same risk — a different hour and a decision that was already made.\n\nThe strategy was never the variable. The trade count was. And you cannot see that in a broker statement, only in a record that knows which trade of the day it was.\n\nProduct example — figures illustrate the feature, not real trader results.\n\n#daytrading #tradingjournal #tradingdiscipline #tradingpsychology #propfirmtrader #riskmanagement",
